# Untracked secret material. Every other file in this
# directory is founder-populated on the staging host and MUST
# NOT be committed. This is the only file in the directory
# that IS committed, and only so git tracks the directory
# itself (an empty directory is not tracked by git, and a
# future PR that adds a tracked file here without first
# removing this .gitignore pattern would commit a real
# secret by accident - this file prevents that).
#
# What lives here (see each PR's own cross-references for
# details; this list is the cross-cutting inventory):
#   * postgres.env     (T04) - POSTGRES_PASSWORD
#   * api.env          (T04) - DATABASE_URL, BASE_URL,
#                              OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI,
#                              SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN,
#                              AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY, etc.
#                              (schema: apps/api/.env.example)
#   * web.env          (T04) - reserved for founder overrides;
#                              the web service currently has
#                              no required runtime env vars,
#                              so this file may be empty or
#                              absent
#   * nginx/cert.pem   (T05) - Cloudflare origin certificate
#   * nginx/key.pem    (T05) - Cloudflare origin private key
#
# Cross-references:
#   * apps/api/.env.example (T01) - schema for api.env
#   * apps/web/.env.example (T01) - schema for web.env
#   * infra/docker-compose.yml (T04) - which env_files are
#     loaded from this directory and in what order compose
#     reads them
#   * VOC-032-R00 (impact-analysis.md) - rationale for
#     keeping SSH keys / TLS material / database
#     credentials out of git
#
# Pattern: `*` ignores every file, `!.gitignore` re-asserts
# that this .gitignore itself stays tracked. The standard
# ignore-everything-except-the-ignore-file pattern.

*
!.gitignore
